And BTW, the 4 line signature limit has everything
to do with bytes, as Boudewijn implies, and nothing
to do with "excess windows", your historical
revisionism.

Windows are virtual, and have been "free" since
paper terminals went away.

Newsreader software has long ago included the
ability to stop reading after any point in the
article, particularly indluding not reading long
siggies.

In contrast the storage of news in spool files, and
the cost of transmitting it to users on slow
interfaces, are both extremely byte-volume sensitive
to this day, despite thousands-fold improvement in
line rates and hard drive capacities.

The four lines weren't ever intended to be room for
some cute quote, it was intended to be room for your
typical college person's contact information,
[building, office number, phone, email address,
office hours, and such] back in those halcyon
pre-spam days when people posting articles _wanted_
contact from those reading what they wrote.



